IMPORT prelude

-- Defence Science and Technology Agency Act 2000 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a person who meets the Agency: the
-- employee's duty to stay on when the Minister requires it and the ban on strikes (s 11), personal immunity (s 12), the Government's
-- share of a transferred employee's pension (s 24(4)), the Agency's symbol (s 31), secrecy (s 32), who may not be a director and the
-- board's quorum (First Schedule paras 10, 12(2)), and the duty to answer the auditor (Second Schedule paras 8, 9).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/DSTAA2000.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the last amending Act in its
-- Legislative History is Act 5 of 2018 (Public Sector (Governance) Act 2018, s 57, in force 1 April 2018). The retrieval record says
-- "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026".
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0165 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. Most of this Act constitutes a statutory board, so the row is SCOPED to the provisions that bind or protect
-- an individual or business: the staff offences, immunity, pension apportionment, the symbol and secrecy offences, director
-- disqualification, the quorum, and the auditor's power to demand information from "any person". Not encoded: incorporation and the
-- seal (ss 3, 4), board size (s 5), functions and powers (ss 6, 7), ministerial directions and delegation (ss 8, 9), the Chief
-- Executive (s 10), the financial provisions (ss 14-21), the 2000 transfer of property, contracts and proceedings (ss 22, 26-29), the
-- rest of the transferred employees' protections (ss 23, 24(1)-(3), (5), 25), the annual report (s 30), regulations (s 33), and the
-- rest of the Schedules. No regulations made under s 33 were retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Defence Science and Technology Agency Act 2000 -- staff and offences`

§§ `11 -- staying on when required, and no strikes`

-- s 11(2): "If it appears to the Minister to be necessary for the public safety, defence or security of Singapore, the Minister may
-- require any employee of the Agency to continue in the employment of the Agency for such period as the Minister may determine, and
-- the employee must continue in the employment of the Agency for that period." (3): the Minister's decision "is final and is not
-- subject to appeal or review in any court".
-- s 11(4): "An employee of the Agency must not go on strike or instigate or incite others to take part in or otherwise act in
-- furtherance of any industrial action." (6): "strike" is "the cessation of work by a body of persons ... acting in combination, or a
-- concerted refusal, or a refusal under a common understanding of a number of persons"; "industrial action" is action "acting in
-- combination or under a common understanding" that would limit, restrict or delay the performance of a duty.
-- s 11(5): "Any employee who fails to comply with a requirement of the Minister under subsection (2) or who contravenes
-- subsection (4)" -- fine not exceeding $2,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 3 years or both. No reasonable-excuse defence is written.
--
-- Joining a concerted go-slow or work-to-rule is read as "otherwise act in furtherance of any industrial action" (a reading of the
-- sentence's grammar). A lone refusal to work is neither a strike nor industrial action, both of which need a body of persons.
DECLARE `Employee conduct` HAS
    `is an employee of the Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister required continued employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `left before the required period ended` IS A BOOLEAN
    `stopped or refused work in combination with others` IS A BOOLEAN
    `incited others to take industrial action` IS A BOOLEAN
    `joined a concerted go-slow or work-to-rule` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the conduct` IS AN `Employee conduct`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee commits an offence under section 11` IF
        `the conduct`'s `is an employee of the Agency`
    AND (    (`the conduct`'s `the Minister required continued employment` AND `the conduct`'s `left before the required period ended`)
         OR  `the conduct`'s `stopped or refused work in combination with others`
         OR  `the conduct`'s `incited others to take industrial action`
         OR  `the conduct`'s `joined a concerted go-slow or work-to-rule`)

§§ `12 -- protection from personal liability`

-- s 12: "No suit or other legal proceedings shall lie personally against any director, officer or employee of the Agency or other
-- person acting under the direction of the Agency for anything which is in good faith done or intended to be done in the execution or
-- purported execution of this Act or any other written law." The Agency itself can be sued (s 3(a)); s 12 protects only the person.
GIVEN `is a director, officer, employee or person acting under the Agency's direction` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `acted in the execution or purported execution of written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is personally immune from suit` IF
        `is a director, officer, employee or person acting under the Agency's direction`
    AND `acted in good faith`
    AND `acted in the execution or purported execution of written law`

§§ `24(4) -- the Government's share of a transferred employee's pension`

-- s 24(4): "the Government is liable to pay to the Agency such portion of any pension, gratuity or allowance payable to such person on
-- his or her retirement as the same bears to the proportion which the aggregate amount of his or her pensionable emoluments during his
-- or her service with the Government or the Singapore Armed Forces ... bears to the aggregate amount of his or her pensionable
-- emoluments during his or her service under both the Government or the Singapore Armed Forces ... and the Agency."
-- The sentence is garbled ("as the same bears to the proportion which"); it is read as: the Government's share is the pension
-- multiplied by Government emoluments over total emoluments. That is a reading, not the words.
GIVEN `the pension` IS A NUMBER, `emoluments in Government service` IS A NUMBER, `emoluments in Agency service` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Government's share of the pension` MEANS
    `the pension` TIMES `emoluments in Government service`
        DIVIDED BY (`emoluments in Government service` PLUS `emoluments in Agency service`)

§§ `31 -- the Agency's symbol`

-- s 31(1): the Agency "has the exclusive right to the use of any symbol or representation that it may select or devise". (2): "Any
-- person who uses a symbol or representation identical with that of the Agency or which so resembles the Agency's symbol or
-- representation as to deceive or cause confusion, or to be likely to deceive or to cause confusion" -- fine not exceeding $10,000 or
-- imprisonment not exceeding 6 months or both. No intent and no registration are required by the words.
GIVEN `used a symbol identical with the Agency's` IS A BOOLEAN, `used a symbol likely to deceive or cause confusion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using the symbol is an offence` IF
    `used a symbol identical with the Agency's` OR `used a symbol likely to deceive or cause confusion`

§§ `32 -- secrecy`

-- s 32(1): "Except for the purpose of the performance of his or her duties or the exercise of his or her functions or when lawfully
-- required to do so by any court or where required or allowed by the provisions of any written law, a person who is or has been a
-- director, an officer, employee, former employee or agent of the Agency or a member of a committee of the Agency must not disclose
-- any information or matter relating to the affairs of the Agency or of any other person which has been obtained by him or her in the
-- performance of his or her duties or the exercise of his or her functions." (2): fine not exceeding $2,000 or imprisonment not
-- exceeding 12 months or both. The duty has no end date: "is or has been".
DECLARE Disclosure HAS
    `is or was a director, officer, employee, agent or committee member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information was obtained in the course of duties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `disclosed for the performance of duties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lawfully required by a court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `required or allowed by written law` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is an offence under section 32` IF
        `the disclosure`'s `is or was a director, officer, employee, agent or committee member`
    AND `the disclosure`'s `the information was obtained in the course of duties`
    AND (NOT `the disclosure`'s `disclosed for the performance of duties`)
    AND (NOT `the disclosure`'s `lawfully required by a court`)
    AND (NOT `the disclosure`'s `required or allowed by written law`)

§§ `Second Schedule paras 8, 9 -- answering the auditor`

-- Para 8: the auditor "may require any person to furnish the auditor with such information in the possession of that person or to
-- which that person has access as the auditor considers necessary ... except where the information pertains to transactions that are
-- declared by the Permanent Secretary to the Ministry of Defence to be of a secret nature."
-- Para 9: "Any person who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with any requirement of the auditor under paragraph 8 or who
-- otherwise hinders, obstructs or delays the auditor" -- fine not exceeding $1,000 and, for a continuing offence, "a further fine not
-- exceeding $100 for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after conviction". No imprisonment.
--
-- "Without reasonable excuse" is read as qualifying only the failure to comply; the second limb repeats "who" and is read as standing
-- alone. A demand for information declared secret is outside para 8, so failing to meet it is read as no breach of a requirement
-- "under paragraph 8". Both are readings.
GIVEN `failed to comply with the auditor's requirement` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the information was declared secret` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `otherwise hindered, obstructed or delayed the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits an offence against the auditor` IF
        (`failed to comply with the auditor's requirement` AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`) AND (NOT `the information was declared secret`))
    OR  `otherwise hindered, obstructed or delayed the auditor`

-- The days counted are days "or part of a day" after conviction; the caller counts a part day as a day.
GIVEN `days or part days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for obstructing the auditor` MEANS
    1000 PLUS 100 TIMES `days or part days continuing after conviction`

§§ `Penalties`

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `leaving when required to stay, or striking (s 11(5))`
    `using the Agency's symbol (s 31(2))`
    `unauthorised disclosure (s 32(2))`
    `obstructing the auditor (Second Schedule para 9)`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `leaving when required to stay, or striking (s 11(5))` THEN 2000
    WHEN `using the Agency's symbol (s 31(2))` THEN 10000
    WHEN `unauthorised disclosure (s 32(2))` THEN 2000
    WHEN `obstructing the auditor (Second Schedule para 9)` THEN 1000

-- Zero means the provision provides no imprisonment.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `leaving when required to stay, or striking (s 11(5))` THEN 36
    WHEN `using the Agency's symbol (s 31(2))` THEN 6
    WHEN `unauthorised disclosure (s 32(2))` THEN 12
    WHEN `obstructing the auditor (Second Schedule para 9)` THEN 0

§§ `First Schedule para 10 -- who may not be a director`

-- Para 10: "A person must not be appointed or continue to hold office as a director if he or she -- (a) has a mental disorder and is
-- incapable of managing himself or herself or his or her affairs; (b) is an undischarged bankrupt or has made any arrangement or
-- composition with his or her creditors; (c) is convicted of an offence involving dishonesty, fraud or moral turpitude and has not
-- received a free pardon; or (d) has been sentenced to imprisonment for a term of 6 months or more and has not received a free pardon."
-- "Has made any arrangement" carries no time limit in the words. One pardon flag covers both (c) and (d) here.
DECLARE `Director candidate` HAS
    `has a mental disorder and is incapable of managing affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has made an arrangement or composition with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `convicted of an offence of dishonesty, fraud or moral turpitude` IS A BOOLEAN
    `longest prison sentence in months` IS A NUMBER
    `received a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the candidate` IS A `Director candidate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate is disqualified from being a director` IF
        `the candidate`'s `has a mental disorder and is incapable of managing affairs`
    OR  `the candidate`'s `is an undischarged bankrupt`
    OR  `the candidate`'s `has made an arrangement or composition with creditors`
    OR  (`the candidate`'s `convicted of an offence of dishonesty, fraud or moral turpitude` AND (NOT `the candidate`'s `received a free pardon`))
    OR  (`the candidate`'s `longest prison sentence in months` AT LEAST 6 AND (NOT `the candidate`'s `received a free pardon`))

§§ `First Schedule para 12(2) -- quorum`

-- Para 12(2): "The quorum at every meeting of the board is one-third of the total number of directors or 3 directors, whichever is the
-- higher." Where one-third is not a whole number the Act does not say how to round; the encoding requires at least one-third present
-- (in effect rounding up). That is an inference. Whether the Chairperson counts among "the total number of directors" is not said;
-- the caller supplies the total.
GIVEN `directors present` IS A NUMBER, `total directors` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the quorum is met` IF
        `directors present` AT LEAST 3
    AND `directors present` TIMES 3 AT LEAST `total directors`
